
2.2.2. Usage of strcpy() function
04:14
Write a C program that reads a string 
 from the user and copies it to another string using the in-built strcpy() function.



Input Format:

A single line containing a string 
 with a maximum length of 99 characters.


#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
	char src[100];  // Source string
	char dest[100]; // Destination string
	
	// Input string from the user
	fgets(src, sizeof(src), stdin);
	src[strcspn(src, "\n")] = '\0'; 



    // Copy string
    strcpy(dest, src);


	// Print the copied string
	printf("%s\n", dest);
	
	return 0;
}


